# Copy to `.env`. Read at BUILD time by Bun and compiled into the client
# bundle, which is the whole difference between this file and `.dev.vars`:
# nothing in here is secret, and nothing in here reaches the Worker.

# Cloudflare Turnstile's *site* key — the public half. Without it the widget
# falls back to Cloudflare's always-passes test key, and since the Worker still
# verifies against the real secret, every write is refused with "could not
# verify you are human". `scripts/prod-setup.sh` sets this and checks the built
# bundle actually carries it.
BUN_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=""

# Overrides the canonical origin in `origin.ts` — for a staging host or a
# preview that should not point crawlers at production.
# SITE_URL="https://wallid.lol"

# Reading `bun run pulse` — how many people are at the wall, and how many came
# in the last hour. Neither is compiled into the bundle: this file is read at
# build time by Bun, and these two are read at *run* time by a script, which is
# why they are safe to keep beside the public ones and why they never reach the
# Worker.
#
# The token is an account token with `Account Analytics: Read`, not the deploy
# token — it can read every Analytics Engine dataset on the account, which is
# exactly why it stays out of the Worker's secrets.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=""
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=""
